[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The board app hard-codes nothing the grammar can say

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BOARD-GRAMMAR-DRIVEN
TITLE: The board app hard-codes nothing the grammar can say
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The board app SHALL contain minimal hard-coded knowledge of the system it
renders: anything the app cannot infer from the grammar is a gap. Two
exceptions are permitted, and both are guarded rather than trusted. Coloring
and styles SHALL be deterministically validated as complete against the
grammar -- every element and role styled, none silently falling to a default
-- and should ideally be literally a CSS sheet. A hand-authored presentation
is allowed where reasoning needs an arrangement the grammar cannot express,
PROVIDED a check guards it: every node type the grammar declares is covered
by the presentation and nothing stale remains in it, checked statically in
nix flake check, with a runtime check on the page as the safety net for a
refresh or reload. The first instance is the Grammars tab's groups
(WORK-GRAMMAR-TAB-GROUPS).
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Hedged by the operator -- verbatim: "one requirement I have we could add is
board (app) should contain minimal hard coded info about the system." Filed
as a REQUIREMENT node at sketch rather than parked as a work item; that
filing (and this node's continued existence) is the carver's resolution of
"we could add", reversible at grooming. Known standing violations to burn
down: TYPE_COLORS in card.js and the duplicated series colors in theme.css
(hard-coded, no completeness check); the Perspective default column lists.

Operator, 2026-09-02, verbatim: "okay I'm going to violate one of my own
proposed rules with justification. the everything must be generated, not
hard coded. justification is I want a check to guard. The grammar page I
want customized for reasoning, it should check every node type is covered
though (ideally a check rather than runtime error alone but runtime is a
good check also as safety check or if I need to refresh/reload)."
